 "prediction_scored": "miss: the adjusted slope is positive (+0.50 F, -0.03 to +1.04), not negative. At NTA level (n=194) it is positive with the interval above 0 (+0.44, +0.15 to +0.73). Vegetative cover (grass and trees, EHDP 2143) has the predicted negative slope (-0.62 F per SD, -1.17 to -0.07).",
 "settle": "Street-tree density per km2 measures how much of an area is street grid, not how much of it is shaded: dense grids (Manhattan, inner Brooklyn) have many street trees per km2 and hot roofs and pavement, while parks, cemeteries and low-rise yards are cool but have few street trees. A canopy measure that includes park and yard trees (LiDAR canopy at tract level, or street trees per km of street), with impervious cover and building density as covariates, would settle whether street trees cool surfaces.",
